| change: One-line change: slightly adjusted the five numeric ensemble weights in the submission command. | score after: 0.81897 (-0.00083)\nv125 -> v126: Add a PET-style inference script that runs checkpoint-averaged predictions (with prompt/mask tokenization), applies optimized rounding with provided weights, and produces a submission to augment the existing ensemble. | change: Adds a new inference script (predict_pet2.py) that: registers extra tokenizer tokens, applies a prompt containing a mask token, builds a Dataset and DataLoader, loads multiple checkpoints of AESRegressionModel, averages their predictions, applies an  | score after: n/a\nv126 -> v127: Ensure model and inputs run on the GPU to avoid device-mismatch errors and to speed up inference. | change: Model is moved to CUDA at creation (.to('cuda')) and input batches are moved to CUDA before calling the model (dict comprehension with v.to('cuda')). | score after: 0.82594\nv127 -> v128: Run an additional inference job (exp302) with specified checkpoints and weights while disabling a previous run, to improve the blended submission score. | change: Added a new notebook cell that runs predict_exp302.py with a config, a list of checkpoint paths and an explicit weights array and save-name; commented out the previous predict_pet2.py cell. This changes which pretrained checkpoints are used for infer | score after: 0.82596 (+0.00002)\nv128 -> v129: Enable a different prediction script (predict_pet2), disable the previous one (predict_exp302), and tweak ensemble weights to improve the final submission score. | change: Commented-out the predict_exp302 prediction call and uncommented/activated predict_pet2; adjusted the last ensemble weight in the predict_pet2 weights list (5.3453 -> 4.87535). | score after: 0.82845 (+0.00249)\nv129 -> v130: Switch the inference to a different set of 'clean' checkpoints and update ensemble weights / script selection to (attempt to) improve the final submission. | change: Uncommented and ran predict_ordinal using checkpoints from exp306b-large-clean-last with updated ensemble weights; commented out a predict_pet2 invocation and changed checkpoint/config paths. | score after: 0.82607 (-0.00238)\nv130 -> v131: Optionally rescale model predictions to match OOF/training distribution (MinMax scaling) before applying optimized ordinal rounding; also update example ensemble weights. | change: Added sklearn MinMaxScaler import and a --do-scale CLI flag. When enabled, concatenates OOF CSVs, fits a MinMaxScaler on them and applies it to preds before rounding/submission. Also updated the example weights in the run command. | score after: n/a\nv131 -> v132: Fix scaler fitting to use the raw prediction column from the oof DataFrame instead of attempting to reshape the DataFrame directly, ensuring correct normalization of predictions. | change: Replaced scaler.fit(oof.reshape(-1, 1)) with scaler.fit(oof[\"raw_pred\"].values.reshape(-1, 1)) to use the 'raw_pred' column for fitting the MinMaxScaler. | score after: n/a\nv132 -> v133: Correct the prediction scaling so normalized model outputs are mapped back to the original score range (scale 0-1 → 1-6) before applying rounding/thresholding. | change: After MinMax scaling, predictions are now multiplied by 5 and shifted by +1 (preds = scaler.transform(...) * 5 + 1) to map the 0–1 normalized outputs back to the 1–6 score range prior to optimized rounding. | score after: 0.82503\nv133 -> v134: Tweak ensemble blend weights and disable input scaling for the prediction run to adjust final submission outputs. | change: Removed the --do-scale flag and replaced the verbose floating-point blend weights with simplified values '[1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5, 5.5]'. | score after: 0.80343 (-0.02159)\nv134 -> v135: Tune the ensemble blending weights used at inference to slightly improve final submission score. | change: Adjusted the blend weights passed to the prediction script from '[1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5, 5.5]' to '[1.65, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5, 5]'. | score after: 0.80784 (+0.00441)\nv135 -> v136: Switch the inference call to a different prediction script and use a different (DeBERTa-v3-small) set of checkpoints/configs for submission generation. | change: Replaced a predict_ordinal.py call (using exp306b large checkpoints and large model path) with predict_separated.py using exp305 DeBERTa-v3-small config and four small-model fold checkpoints; updated model.path to deberta-v3-small and slightly reform | score after: 0.80526 (-0.00258)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
